window.docContents[242].resolve({"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Core/#LindenstraussPolynomials___etaV":{"contents":"The error term η'_m of eq:vordered. \n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.etaV","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Core/#LindenstraussPolynomials___etaV"},"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Theorems/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Theorems-1-0":{"contents":"Main results\n\n* Lemma lem:isometry: the canonical extension preserves the norm, for scalar- and vector-valued polynomials.* Theorem thm:main: for every continuous n-homogeneous scalar polynomial P (n\\ge1) and every \\varepsilon>0 there are Q and z in the unit ball of X^{**} with \\|Q-P\\|<\\varepsilon and |\\widetilde Q(z)|=\\|\\widetilde Q\\|=\\|Q\\|; equivalently, such polynomials are dense.* Theorem thm:vector: the same for polynomials with values in a Banach space Y.\n\nHere \\|\\widetilde Q\\| is the supremum of \\|\\widetilde Q(z)\\| over the closed unit ball of the bidual. X need not be complete; only Y is assumed complete in the vector-valued case.\n\n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.Theorems","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Theorems/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Theorems-1-0"}});